{
  "retrieved": "2026-10-18",
  "coverage": "Seven regions and the two cities of republican significance, Bishkek and Osh, with English, Kyrgyz and Russian names. Retained OpenStreetMap relation geometry is community mapped, not an official cadastral boundary. It does not fully reflect the 2024 city expansions; approximate city geometry is explicitly identified, and city mapped area/density are omitted. Official NSC 1 January 2026 populations sum exactly to 7,404,329; regional areas use rounded published total administrative territory, including water. A detailed-level audit found 39 of 40 official rayons plus incomplete city coverage and outdated names, so that incomplete layer is not exposed. Current NSC administrative structure and Manas city rename are checked against primary publications. Issyk-Kul, Song-Kul, Chatyr-Kul and reservoirs are removed from land fills. Complete shared frontiers follow existing atlas Kazakhstan and China geometry. Foreign enclaves in the retained source remain outside Kyrgyz land.",
  "counts": {
    "1": 9
  },
  "processing": "Full available source resolution retained, cleaned together and rounded to six decimal places. Shared internal edges stored once; unselected coasts have no stroke. Deeper geometry loads only for the selected region. All views use the shared regional renderer, selected-outline index, adaptive detail, lifecycle and three-country cache. Territorial waters are excluded from land fills. Territory context features carry their own destination bounds.",
